From 7756dd126ebd4e09c750124e8592c1dda6e0d777 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:00:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix change detection, add guides/routes/digest archive,
 expand thin pages

Addresses the AdSense "low value content" rejection and the 16 area pages sitting
in Search Console under "Discovered - currently not indexed".

Data integrity
- scraper.py: replace raw-byte hashing with a content signal (title + h1-h4 +
  link text). The old approach flagged ~120 of 223 galleries as changed EVERY DAY
  (~54%), which is noise from rotating nonces and cache-busting build hashes, not
  exhibitions. Falls back to normalized text, then raw bytes, and re-baselines
  safely without flagging everything on first run.
- validate_data.py: new. Catches malformed URLs, out-of-city coordinates,
  borough/coordinate disagreement, duplicates, and unqualified addresses.
- fix_geocoding.py: new. Repairs ~30 Tribeca/SoHo galleries whose bare addresses
  geocoded to same-named Brooklyn streets, putting them 3-6 km from their real
  locations and on the wrong borough and neighborhood pages.
- Fixed 2 malformed gallery URLs that rendered as broken relative links.

New content
- visiting-nyc-galleries.html: first-timer's guide (~1,150 words).
- routes/: 9 walking routes ordered by nearest-neighbour + 2-opt over the real
  coordinates, with per-district practical notes.
- new-shows/: permanent weekly digest archive, one dated page per week, with a
  plausibility ceiling that refuses to publish an implausible number.

Expanded pages
- Bronx, Staten Island, Queens, East Village, Greenpoint and Bushwick grew from
  206-338 words to 655-847, with original editorial rather than padding.

Plumbing
- site_common.py: shared page shell so every generated page matches.
- build_site.py: runs the generators in dependency order.
- sitemap.xml now discovers guides, routes and digests from disk (30 URLs, was 18).
- about.html and privacy.html gained missing description and canonical tags.
