+    <h1>A walking route through Lower East Side's art galleries</h1>
+    <p class="intro">A 12-stop walking route through the art galleries of Lower East Side, ordered so you walk 1.2 mi instead of doubling back.</p>
+    <ul class="stats">
+      <li><strong>12</strong><span>galleries</span></li>
+      <li><strong>1.2 mi</strong><span>total walking</span></li>
+      <li><strong>25 min</strong><span>walking time, not counting stops</span></li>
+    </ul>
+      <p>The Lower East Side has the highest gallery-per-block density in the city outside Chelsea, and the spaces are small enough that you can see a show properly in five minutes. That makes this the single best route for anyone who wants to see a lot of art in one afternoon.</p>
+      <p>The galleries here tend to show younger and less established artists than the uptown rooms, which means a higher variance in what you find and a better chance of seeing something before anyone else does.</p>
+    <p><strong>Getting to the start:</strong> F to Delancey St, J/M/Z to Essex St, or B/D to Grand St.</p>
+    <p>Lower East Side has 29 galleries on our map. This route takes the 12 that sit closest together — the walkable core of the district — because a 29-stop walk is a list, not a route. The <a href="/galleries/lower-east-side.html">full Lower East Side directory</a> has the rest.</p>
