+    <h1>A walking route through Upper East Side's art galleries</h1>
+    <p class="intro">A 12-stop walking route through the art galleries of Upper East Side, ordered so you walk 1.3 mi instead of doubling back.</p>
+    <ul class="stats">
+      <li><strong>12</strong><span>galleries</span></li>
+      <li><strong>1.3 mi</strong><span>total walking</span></li>
+      <li><strong>27 min</strong><span>walking time, not counting stops</span></li>
+    </ul>
+      <p>The most genteel of the routes, threading through townhouses and side streets off Madison Avenue. The galleries here deal largely in modern, postwar and secondary-market work, which means you will see more historically significant art and fewer surprises than downtown.</p>
+      <p>The route sits within a few blocks of Museum Mile, so it combines naturally with the Met, the Guggenheim, the Frick or the Neue Galerie. Doing both in a day makes for a long but coherent walk.</p>
+    <p><strong>Getting to the start:</strong> 4/5/6 to 77th or 86th St, or Q to 72nd or 86th St.</p>
+    <p>Upper East Side has 17 galleries on our map. This route takes the 12 that sit closest together — the walkable core of the district — because a 17-stop walk is a list, not a route. The <a href="/galleries/upper-east-side.html">full Upper East Side directory</a> has the rest.</p>
+    <h2>Practical notes for this walk</h2>
+      <p><strong>Best time to go.</strong> Tuesday to Friday. Weekend hours are shorter here than downtown, and some spaces close Saturdays in summer.</p>
+      <p><strong>Worth knowing.</strong> Several galleries here occupy townhouses and upper floors and operate partly by appointment. A call ahead is more useful in this district than any other.</p>
+      <p><strong>Combine it with.</strong> Museum Mile is a few blocks west. The Met, the Guggenheim, the Frick and the Neue Galerie are all within reach of this route.</p>
